/-!
# Exceptional branches in the first construction of 13.6.13

Both native exceptional alternatives are excluded under the genuine marked
local setup. The outer proof applies the parity restriction to the
two-residual of the actual L*_v intersection with the offender subgroup.
It obtains L*_v = X and its moved plane, contradicting the earlier relative
nonnormality of V_v. Every quotient map and Sylow intersection is literal.

The five-input recovery adapter discharges the recovered-action premise.
The factor-construction consumer retains the full S₃, two-factor, and
hyperplane alternatives. The earlier source inputs and adequate classifier
remain with final assembly; no factor decomposition or exclusion is assumed.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
13.6.13, printed p.929, and B.5.1 / B.5.6–7, pp.99, 105–106.
